Under `inline_steps` the bodies are rendered at compose time, so a Jinja failure in one is a
blocking notice like any other rather than a `**STOP` buried inside a single step's section: the
step table and every section — including the healthy step's — are withheld, and the exit code stays
0.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inline-broken/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-inline-broken
title: Inline Broken
summary: An embedded body that cannot render.
jinja: true
inline_steps: true
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inline-broken/playbook.yaml --
graph:
  one: []
  two: [one]
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inline-broken/one/prompt.md --
---
name: one
summary: Broken step.
---

{% include "nope.md" %}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-inline-broken/two/prompt.md --
---
name: two
summary: Healthy step.
---

Two body.
-- cmd --
booping render-playbook fx-inline-broken
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
**STOP — tell the user:** Jinja rendering of step 'one' failed: TemplateNotFound: nope.md. Do not execute this playbook.

Preamble.
-- stderr --
